Package: calamares-settings-linus
Version: 1.0.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: linus contributors <kevinthelago@gmail.com>
Depends: calamares (>= 3.2),
         linus-branding,
         python3-pyaml,
         kpartx,
         grub-efi-amd64 [amd64] | grub-pc,
         dosfstools,
         squashfs-tools,
         gptfdisk | gdisk,
         efibootmgr [amd64],
         cage,
         gtkgreet,
         greetd
Recommends: btrfs-progs, xfsprogs, cryptsetup-bin
Description: Calamares installer settings for linus
 Branded configuration for the Calamares graphical installer,
 pre-configured for the linus Debian-based distribution. Installs
 the linus desktop from a live squashfs image to disk, supporting
 UEFI and BIOS boot, optional LUKS full-disk encryption, and
 configures greetd with the mantle Wayland session as default.
 .
 This package is intended to be installed only in the live image
 and is removed from the target system by the installer itself.
